edWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="https://mobile.twitter.com" rel="nofollow">Twitter Web App</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4Nzc5NzA2NTg4NzA2NDQ3Mzg=', 'text': 'I was repeatedly suspended by Facebook for questioning the need to vaccinate children against Covid-19. My posts about the Covid vaccine rollout to children in the UK (both on Facebook and Twitter) were used as evidence by anonymous whistleblowers to complain to my employer and eventually end my successful career as a headteacher.\n\nMark Zuckerberg is simply jumping on the bandwagon of the US election result, while simultaneously keeping a foot in the camp of censorship and Big Pharma shilling.\n\nThe points which I would repeat on Facebook and Twitter were as follows:\n\n1) Children are at extremely low risk of serious illness from Covid.\n\n2) The Covid vaccines pose known, very serious risks.\n\n3) There is no long-term safety data for the Covid vaccines.\n\n4) A child can still catch and spread Covid when vaccinated against the virus.\n\nI would then say that, in my personal opinion, the risks from the Covid vaccines outweigh any possible benefit to a child. I would also post the picture below.\n\nFacebook said that this was medical misinformation and repeatedly censored me for it. \n\nMark Zuckerberg had a golden opportunity to do something great for humanity and particularly for our children\'s health and wellbeing. However, he failed to do the right thing and continues to do so by propping up the now debunked "safe and effective" mantra. \n\nDo not fall for his attempt to rebrand himself as one of the good guys. His stance on the Covid vaccines is clear evidence to the contrary.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Sat Jan 11 06:47:50 +0000 2025', 'conv